'use strict';
let focusProgress={};try{const p=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('spotmatch-focus-v1')||'{}');if(p&&typeof p==='object'&&!Array.isArray(p))focusProgress=p;}catch{}
let focusState=null;
function focusSave(){try{localStorage.setItem('spotmatch-focus-v1',JSON.stringify(focusProgress));}catch{}}
function focusLinks(keys){return `<ul class="sen-sources">${keys.map(key=>{const s=focusSources[key];return `<li><a href="${s.url}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">${s.title} ↗</a><p>${s.note}</p></li>`;}).join('')}</ul>`;}
function focusParentGuide(){return `<h3>ADHD and ADD: what do these names mean?</h3><p>ADHD is a neurodevelopmental condition. Children can have mainly inattentive difficulties, mainly hyperactive-impulsive difficulties, or both. “ADD” is an older term commonly used for the predominantly inattentive presentation. A child who is quiet, daydreams, or struggles to begin may need just as much support as a child who is visibly restless. This course welcomes either profile; a diagnosis is not required.</p><p>Inattention, impulsive actions, and activity level vary between children and situations. ADHD is not diagnosed by poor performance in a game. Developmental stage, difficulties understanding instructions, sleep, anxiety, hearing, vision, sensory demands, and motor access can also affect participation. Persistent difficulties across everyday settings are a reason to discuss individual assessment and support with the child’s professional team. <a href="${focusSources.overview.url}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the NIMH overview ↗</a></p><h3>Why “try harder to concentrate” may not help</h3><p>A task can ask a child to hold the goal in mind, ignore competing details, organise several actions, and shift to a new activity—all at once. Our design makes some of those demands visible. A picture reminder can hold the plan; a clear next step can make beginning easier. Being deeply engaged in a favourite activity does not mean the child can summon the same attention for every task. We do not measure eye contact, sitting still, or how quickly the child clicks.</p><h3>What we are trying to develop</h3><p>The exercises offer supported practice comparing a choice with a goal, referring to a visible plan, checking a selection, taking one step, and returning after a pause. The aim is participation in meaningful activities. Our sequence and suggested short sets are design choices, not a validated ADHD programme or a prescribed dose. Learning a game does not prove improved attention elsewhere.</p><h3>Which teaching features have a research or guidance basis?</h3><p>Clinical and educational guidance supports adapting tasks and environments to the child. We use small achievable steps, clear goals, external reminders, and a predictable way to continue. These are accommodations and teaching supports; using them is not a failure to learn. NICE describes individual environmental modifications within a broader care plan. <a href="${focusSources.environment.url}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NICE guidance ↗</a></p><p>CDC guidance describes clear expectations, prompt positive feedback, shorter tasks, breaks, and help with organisation, while noting that evidence for particular accommodations varies. Our feedback names the task outcome, and children can revise choices. We do not use lost lives, public rankings, streak pressure, or withdrawal of breaks. <a href="${focusSources.classroom.url}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CDC classroom guidance ↗</a></p><h3>Can computer games improve ADHD or everyday focus?</h3><p>Some training improves performance on the skill practised. Transfer to different tasks, classroom learning, ADHD symptoms, and everyday functioning is a separate question. A 2023 meta-analysis of randomised cognitive-training trials found limited clinical transfer, including no clear effect on total ADHD symptoms in probably blinded ratings. This is why we do not market our games as an ADHD treatment, attention test, or proven way to improve reading. Much of the training research involves school-aged children; it does not establish benefits for preschoolers or this letter-free format. Our particular games have not been evaluated. <a href="${focusSources.training.url}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the cognitive-training review ↗</a></p><h3>A comfortable way to use this course</h3><ol><li>Choose a game the child understands and finds interesting. An adult models one example using speech, sign, pointing, or the child’s usual AAC.</li><li>Choose one exploration or a small set. There is no timer and no recommended daily quota. Stop sooner if the child communicates that they have had enough.</li><li>Keep the goal visible. Try fewer pictures or a shorter instruction. If support helps, keep it rather than repeatedly testing without it.</li><li>Give concrete feedback: “You checked the picture plan” or “We found the next step.” Respond warmly to requests for help and breaks.</li><li>Try a similar practical task away from the screen. Ask whether the same reminder or smaller step helps. Repeated game success alone is not evidence of everyday improvement.</li></ol><h3>Movement, breaks, and returning</h3><p>A break is available at any point; it does not have to be earned by finishing. The pause screen preserves the current task while this page remains open. Choose rest, company, communication, or a familiar comfortable movement with the child’s usual supports. No pose, breathing routine, or movement is mandatory.</p><p>Structured physical-activity programmes have been studied in ADHD, with promising but variable findings. A brief break here is not equivalent to those programmes, and an individual child may prefer a different kind of pause. <a href="${focusSources.movement.url}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the exercise review ↗</a></p><h3>What should parents notice?</h3><p>Look for useful changes in real activities: beginning a small task with a clearer cue, consulting a reminder, choosing help, or returning with support. Distinguish help understanding the goal from help operating the screen. A slower response is not worse focus. Notice frustration, fatigue, and the child’s preferences as well as completed steps. No symptom, concentration, or ability score is generated.</p><h3>How this fits with wider support</h3><p>These games supplement appropriate educational and clinical care. Parent training in behaviour management and classroom interventions are structured approaches delivered with professional support; our parent notes are not a substitute for that training. Choices about ADHD treatment belong with the family and the child’s clinician. <a href="${focusSources.parents.url}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CDC parent-training explanation ↗</a></p><h3>Parent reading and research</h3>${focusLinks(Object.keys(focusSources))}<p class="micro">Choose by the individual child’s needs. No child name or diagnosis is collected. The app saves only which focus games were explored, separately from other courses.</p>`;}
const focusLibraryBefore=libraryHome;
libraryHome=function(){focusLibraryBefore();const section=document.createElement('section');section.id='focus-trail';section.className='calm-library focus-library';section.innerHTML=`<div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">ONE HELPFUL STEP AT A TIME</span><h2>A little support for attention.</h2></div><span class="micro">20 new games</span></div><button class="calm-banner focus-banner" id="focusOpen"><div><span class="adult-badge">Play together</span><h2>The Little Focus Trail</h2><p>Keep a picture plan nearby. Check a clue. Take a break whenever you need.</p><span>Explore the trail →</span><small class="sen-audience">For grown-ups · ADHD, including inattentive ADHD often called ADD</small></div><div class="calm-banner-art" aria-hidden="true">${friendlyCover('events')}</div></button>`;app.append(section);document.querySelector('#focusOpen').onclick=focusHome;const a=document.createElement('a');a.href='#focus-trail';a.className='sen-shortcut';a.textContent='Explore focus games & ADHD / ADD guidance ↓';app.querySelector('.welcome-copy')?.append(a);};
function focusNav(){document.querySelector('#libraryNav').onclick=libraryHome;document.querySelector('#brand').onclick=e=>{e.preventDefault();libraryHome();};document.querySelector('#courseNav').onclick=focusHome;document.querySelector('#guideNav').onclick=()=>{focusHome();const el=document.querySelector('#focusGuide');el.open=true;el.scrollIntoView();};}
function focusHome(){activeLearningCourse=null;senActive=null;const done=Object.values(focusProgress).filter(x=>x?.explored).length;app.innerHTML=`<div class="play-top"><button class="back" id="focusLibrary">← Our adventures</button><span class="together-note">♧ An adult joins in</span></div><section class="course-hero friendly-course-hero focus-hero"><div><span class="eyebrow">PICTURE PLANS · CLEAR CLUES · ROOM TO PAUSE</span><h1>The Little Focus Trail</h1><p>One helpful step. A little checking. Your way back after a break.</p><button class="primary" id="focusStart">Choose a little game ↓</button><span class="micro course-smallprint">20 games · Choose one exploration or a short set</span></div><div class="course-hero-art" aria-hidden="true">${friendlyCover('events')}</div></section><details class="course-about" id="focusGuide"><summary><span>For grown-ups · ADHD & ADD</span><span class="about-subtitle">Understanding attention, practical support, evidence & parent reading</span><span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><div class="sen-parent-copy focus-parent">${focusParentGuide()}</div></details><section id="focusGames"><div class="section-head"><h2>What shall we explore?</h2><span class="micro">${done} of 20 explored</span></div><div class="grid friendly-game-grid">${focusGames.map((d,i)=>`<button class="course-card" data-focus-game="${i}"><div class="thumb" style="--tint:#e4ebdf">${pictureIcon(['cup','train','leaf','bowl','apple','flower','basket','umbrella','spoon','book','brush','carrot','hat','butterfly','paper','basket','bee','rabbit','chair','tree'][i])}${focusProgress[i]?.explored?'<span class="played-mark" aria-label="Explored">✓</span>':''}</div><span class="card-num">${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><h3>${d.title}</h3><span class="card-bottom">Explore together →</span></button>`).join('')}</div></section><p class="note">No timer, speed score, or requirement to sit still. Help, AAC, movement, and breaks stay available. Game practice is not a proven treatment for ADHD.</p><details class="quiet-notes"><summary>Progress on this device</summary><p>Only explored focus-game numbers are saved. Ending early is fine. No concentration, symptom, or performance score is stored.</p><button class="secondary" id="focusReset">Clear Focus Trail progress</button></details>`;focusNav();document.querySelector('#focusLibrary').onclick=libraryHome;document.querySelector('#focusStart').onclick=()=>document.querySelector('#focusGames').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'});document.querySelectorAll('[data-focus-game]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>focusIntro(+b.dataset.focusGame));document.querySelector('#focusReset').onclick=()=>{focusProgress={};focusSave();focusHome();};window.scrollTo(0,0);}
function focusIntro(index){focusState={index,round:0,total:3,seed:nextPictureVisit('focus',index),fewer:true,task:null,selected:[],done:false,help:false,paused:false,plan:[null,null,null],message:''};const d=focusGames[index];app.innerHTML=`<div class="play-top"><button class="back" id="focusBack">← Our focus trail</button><span class="together-note">♧ Play together</span></div><section class="game-wrap friendly-play focus-play"><h1>${d.title}</h1><p>${d.skill}</p><div class="game-stage"><div class="adult-demo-picture">${pictureIcon(['cup','train','leaf','bowl','apple','flower','basket','umbrella','spoon','book','brush','carrot','hat','butterfly','paper','basket','bee','rabbit','chair','tree'][index])}</div><p>One small exploration, or a short set? You can stop or pause at any time.</p><div class="calm-controls"><button class="secondary" id="focusOne">One little exploration</button><button class="primary" id="focusThree">A set of three</button></div></div><details class="quiet-notes"><summary>A little tip for grown-ups</summary><p>${d.tip}</p><p>An adult models the meaning first. No voice is generated; the child can point, sign, speak, or use AAC.</p></details></section>`;focusNav();document.querySelector('#focusBack').onclick=focusHome;document.querySelector('#focusOne').onclick=()=>{focusState.total=1;focusPlay();};document.querySelector('#focusThree').onclick=focusPlay;window.scrollTo(0,0);}
function focusMakeTask(index,round,seed=0){const d=focusGames[index],n=(seed*3+round)%9;let t={mode:d.mode,reference:[],inventory:[],options:[],answer:[],instruction:'Explore together.',response:[]};const options=(correct,others)=>{t.options=shuffle([{id:'yes',picture:correct},...others.map((picture,i)=>({id:'no'+i,picture}))]);t.answer=['yes'];};
 if(d.mode==='select'){const bank=d.theme==='cup'?wordPictureBank.kitchen:d.theme==='toys'?wordPictureBank.toys:d.theme==='helpers'?wordPictureBank.helpers:wordPictureBank.clothing;const id=bank[n%bank.length];t.reference=[id];options(id,[bank[(n+1)%bank.length],bank[(n+3)%bank.length]]);t.instruction='Look at our model. Choose its matching picture, then check.';}
 if(['shape','two','switch'].includes(d.mode)){const leaf=(shape,color)=>({calmLeaf:shape,color}),green='#86a28a',gold='#d3b46e';if(d.mode==='two'){const id=['cup','bowl','apple'][(seed+round)%3];const attr=(size,full)=>id==='cup'?{type:'attribute',attr:'two',size,full}:{type:'attribute',attr:'size',object:id,value:size};const target=attr(round%2?'big':'small',true);t.reference=[target];options(target,id==='cup'?[attr(round%2?'small':'big',true),attr(round%2?'big':'small',false)]:[attr(round%2?'small':'big',true),{icon:id==='apple'?'pear':'plate'}]);t.instruction=id==='cup'?'Check the cup’s size and whether it is full. Which picture matches both?':'Check the object and its size. Which picture matches both?';}else{const useColor=d.mode==='switch'&&round%2===1,target=leaf(0,green);t.reference=[target];options(useColor?leaf(1,green):leaf(0,gold),[useColor?leaf(0,gold):leaf(1,green),leaf(1,gold)]);t.instruction=useColor?'New clue: match the colour. The shape may be different.':'Our clue: match the leaf shape. The colour may be different.';}}
 if(['collect','checklist','missing'].includes(d.mode)){const ids=d.theme==='rain'?['coat','umbrella','shoe']:d.theme==='food'?['apple','bread','cheese']:['cup','spoon','apple'];const targets=ids.slice(0,round===2?3:2);t.reference=targets;if(d.mode==='missing'){const missing=targets[round%targets.length];t.inventory=targets.filter(x=>x!==missing);options(missing,['ball','key']);t.instruction='Our plan is above. These things are already packed below it. Which planned thing is still missing?';}else{t.options=shuffle([...targets.map((picture,i)=>({id:'target'+i,picture})),{id:'extra',picture:d.theme==='rain'?'ball':'hat'}]);t.answer=targets.map((_,i)=>'target'+i);t.instruction='Use the picture plan. Choose each planned item, then check. You can change your choices.';}}
 if(d.mode==='route'){const ids=d.theme==='return'?['book','cup','flower']:['seed','wateringcan','sprout'];t.reference=ids;t.options=ids.map((picture,i)=>({id:String(i),picture}));t.answer=ids.map((_,i)=>String(i));t.instruction='Follow the highlighted next picture, one step at a time. A break keeps your place.';}
 if(d.mode==='order'){const ids=d.theme==='supported'?[['cup','spoon'],['hat','shoe'],['book','ball']][(seed+round)%3]:d.theme==='three'?['cup','spoon','apple']:['spoon','bowl'];t.reference=ids;t.options=shuffle([...ids.map((picture,i)=>({id:String(i),picture})),{id:'extra',picture:'key'}]);t.answer=ids.map((_,i)=>String(i));t.instruction='Follow this picture plan from left to right. Choose the pictures in that order, then check.';}
 if(d.mode==='classify'){const target=['apple','carrot','ball'][(seed+round)%3];t.reference=['apple','carrot'];t.inventory=[target];t.options=[{id:'keep',picture:'basket',label:'Put in our food basket'},{id:'leave',picture:'tray',label:'Leave on the tray'}];t.answer=[target==='ball'?'leave':'keep'];t.instruction='Our rule is food for the basket. Look at the new item. Put it in the basket, or leave it on the tray.';}
 if(d.mode==='strategy'){const help=d.theme==='help';t.options=(help?['book','cup','rabbit']:['chair','tree','rabbit']).map((picture,i)=>({id:String(i),picture:help?{supportChoice:i}:picture,label:(help?['Show another example','Fewer things at once','Play with a grown-up']:['Rest or watch','A familiar movement','Company or communication'])[i]}));t.mode='open';t.instruction=help?'What kind of help would you like? Choose together; every option is welcome.':'Choose a comfortable kind of break. You can pause right now.';t.response=help?['An adult can model one example, then let you try with help.','Show one or two real objects, or simplify the next instruction.','Explore alongside a grown-up using your usual communication.']:['Rest or watch something familiar. No closed eyes or stillness needed.','Use a familiar comfortable movement with usual supports, or imagine it.','Invite company or keep your usual AAC available.'];}
 if(d.mode==='plan'){t.instruction='Choose a little task, a helpful support, and an ending. You can skip any part.';t.banks=[['book','basket'],['paper','rabbit'],['chair','tree']];t.labels=[['Look at a book','Pack two things'],['Keep a picture plan','Get grown-up help'],['Rest or watch','A comfortable movement']];}
 return t;}
function focusPlay(){const s=focusState;s.task=focusMakeTask(s.index,s.round,s.seed);Object.assign(s,{selected:[],done:false,help:false,paused:false,plan:[null,null,null],message:''});focusRender();window.scrollTo(0,0);}
function focusPicture(p){if(p?.supportChoice!==undefined&&typeof worldHelpArt==='function')return worldHelpArt(p.supportChoice);return p?.calmLeaf!==undefined?calmPicture(p):adultPicture(p);}
function focusVisibleOptions(s){const t=s.task;if(!s.fewer||!['select','shape','switch','two','missing'].includes(t.mode))return t.options;const keep=t.options.filter(o=>t.answer.includes(o.id)),other=t.options.find(o=>!t.answer.includes(o.id));return t.options.filter(o=>keep.includes(o)||o===other);}
function focusRender(focus){const s=focusState,t=s.task,d=focusGames[s.index];if(s.paused){app.innerHTML=`<section class="game-wrap friendly-play focus-play"><div class="completion-friend">${friendlyMascot()}</div><h1>There is room for a pause.</h1><p>Your current pictures and place are waiting while this page stays open.</p><p>Rest, use your communication support, enjoy company, or choose a familiar comfortable movement. No movement is required.</p><div class="calm-controls"><button class="primary" id="focusResume">Return to our place →</button><button class="secondary" id="focusStop">Finish for now</button></div></section>`;focusNav();document.querySelector('#focusResume').onclick=()=>{s.paused=false;focusRender('focusBreak');};document.querySelector('#focusStop').onclick=focusHome;document.querySelector('#focusResume').focus();return;}
 let body=t.reference.length?`<div class="focus-goal"><span class="micro">${t.mode==='classify'?'Our food rule':'Our picture plan / model'}</span><div class="focus-strip">${t.reference.map((p,i)=>`<div class="story-frame">${focusPicture(p)}${['order','route'].includes(t.mode)?`<small>${i+1}</small>`:''}</div>`).join('')}</div></div>`:'';
 if(t.inventory.length)body+=`<div class="focus-inventory"><span class="micro">${t.mode==='classify'?'Our new item':'Already packed'}</span><div class="focus-strip">${t.inventory.map(p=>`<div class="story-frame">${focusPicture(p)}</div>`).join('')}</div></div>`;
 if(t.mode==='open'){const chosen=t.options.find(o=>s.selected.includes(o.id));body+=`<div class="focus-choice-home tp-answer-pad ${chosen?'has-choice':''}" role="group" aria-label="Your choice"><span class="choice-home-heading">Your choice</span>${chosen?`<div class="choice-home-pictures"><div>${focusPicture(chosen.picture)}<span>${senEscape(chosen.label||'Your choice')}</span></div></div>`:'<span>Drag a picture here, or tap one below.</span>'}</div>`;}
 if(t.mode==='plan')body+=`<div class="calm-routine">${t.banks.map((bank,r)=>`<fieldset><legend>${['A little task','A helpful support','A comfortable ending'][r]}</legend>${bank.map((p,i)=>`<button class="secondary ${s.plan[r]===i?'selected':''}" data-focus-plan="${r}:${i}" aria-pressed="${s.plan[r]===i}" ${s.done?'disabled':''}>${focusPicture(p)}<span>${t.labels[r][i]}</span></button>`).join('')}<button class="back" data-focus-plan="${r}:2" aria-pressed="${s.plan[r]===2}" ${s.done?'disabled':''}>Skip this part</button></fieldset>`).join('')}</div>`;
 else body+=`<div class="learning-options focus-options">${focusVisibleOptions(s).map(o=>`<button class="learning-option ${s.selected.includes(o.id)?'selected':''} ${s.help&&t.answer.includes(o.id)?'hinted':''} ${t.mode==='route'&&t.answer[s.selected.length]===o.id?'hinted':''}" data-focus-choice="${o.id}" aria-pressed="${s.selected.includes(o.id)}" aria-label="${senEscape(o.label||('Picture: '+(typeof o.picture==='string'?nameOf(o.picture):o.picture.calmLeaf!==undefined?'leaf':senDescription(o.picture))))}" ${s.done||(t.mode==='order'&&s.selected.includes(o.id))||(t.mode==='route'&&t.answer[s.selected.length]!==o.id)?'disabled':''}>${focusPicture(o.picture)}${o.label?`<small>${o.label}</small>`:''}</button>`).join('')}</div>`;
 if(t.mode==='order')body+=`<div class="focus-strip focus-chosen" aria-label="Your chosen order">${t.answer.map((_,i)=>`<div class="story-frame">${s.selected[i]!==undefined?focusPicture(t.options.find(o=>o.id===s.selected[i]).picture):`<span>${i+1}</span>`}</div>`).join('')}</div>`;
 const ready=t.mode==='route'?s.selected.length===t.answer.length:t.mode==='plan'?s.plan.every(x=>x!==null):s.selected.length>0;
 app.innerHTML=`<div class="play-top"><button class="back" id="focusBack">← Our focus trail</button><span class="together-note">♧ Play together</span></div><section class="game-wrap friendly-play focus-play"><span class="eyebrow">${s.round+1} OF ${s.total} LITTLE EXPLORATIONS</span><h1>${d.title}</h1><p class="play-invitation">${t.instruction}</p><div class="game-stage">${body}<div class="feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite">${senEscape(s.message)}</div><div class="calm-controls">${!s.done?`${['select','shape','switch','two','missing'].includes(t.mode)?`<button class="secondary" id="focusFewer">${s.fewer?'Show three pictures':'Show two pictures'}</button>`:''}<button class="secondary" id="focusHelp">A helping hand</button><button class="secondary" id="focusClear">${t.mode==='open'?'Clear choice':'Change / start again'}</button><button class="primary" id="focusCheck" ${ready?'':'disabled'}>${['open','plan'].includes(t.mode)?'We explored this →':'Check with our plan ✓'}</button>`:`<button class="primary" id="focusNext">${s.round+1===s.total?'Finish this little set →':'Another little exploration →'}</button>`}</div></div><div class="calm-controls"><button class="secondary" id="focusBreak">Take a break</button><button class="back" id="focusStop">Finish for now</button></div><details class="quiet-notes" id="focusTip"><summary>A little tip for grown-ups</summary><p>${d.skill}</p><p>${d.tip}</p><p>Look back at the picture plan whenever useful. No speech, eye contact, stillness, speed, or unsupported performance is required.</p></details><details class="quiet-notes"><summary>Try this in everyday play</summary><p>${d.away}</p></details><details class="quiet-notes"><summary>Why this feature? Research & limits</summary><p>This activity adapts a teaching or support principle; it is not an evaluated ADHD exercise. Completing it does not establish better everyday attention. Our games are supplementary and do not replace appropriate care.</p>${focusLinks(d.sources)}</details></section>`;focusNav();
 const bind=(id,fn)=>{const el=document.getElementById(id);if(el)el.onclick=fn;};bind('focusBack',focusHome);bind('focusStop',focusHome);bind('focusBreak',()=>{s.paused=true;focusRender();});
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-focus-choice]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{const id=b.dataset.focusChoice;if(t.mode==='order'||t.mode==='route')s.selected.push(id);else if(t.mode==='collect'||t.mode==='checklist')s.selected=s.selected.includes(id)?s.selected.filter(x=>x!==id):[...s.selected,id];else s.selected=[id];s.message=t.mode==='open'?t.response[+id]:'';focusRender(t.mode==='route'?'choice:'+t.answer[s.selected.length]:'choice:'+id);});
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-focus-plan]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{const[r,i]=b.dataset.focusPlan.split(':').map(Number);s.plan[r]=i;focusRender('plan:'+b.dataset.focusPlan);});
 bind('focusFewer',()=>{s.fewer=!s.fewer;s.selected=[];s.message='';focusRender('focusFewer');});bind('focusHelp',()=>{s.help=true;s.message=t.mode==='open'||t.mode==='plan'?'Explore the choices with your grown-up. Every preference is welcome.':'Here is a helping hand. Compare the highlighted choices with the picture plan.';focusRender('focusHelp');document.querySelector('#focusTip').open=true;});
 bind('focusClear',()=>{s.selected=[];s.plan=[null,null,null];s.message='';focusRender('focusClear');});bind('focusCheck',()=>{const ok=['open','plan'].includes(t.mode)||(t.mode==='order'||t.mode==='route'?JSON.stringify(s.selected)===JSON.stringify(t.answer):s.selected.length===t.answer.length&&s.selected.every(x=>t.answer.includes(x)));if(ok){s.done=true;s.message=['open','plan'].includes(t.mode)?'A useful choice to share with your grown-up.':'You checked with our plan. Another step or a pause?';}else{s.message='Let’s compare with the plan together. You can change a choice or ask for help.';if(t.mode==='order')s.selected=[];}focusRender(ok?'focusNext':'focusCheck');});
 bind('focusNext',()=>{if(s.round+1===s.total)focusFinish();else{s.round++;focusPlay();}});
 if(focus){let el=focus.startsWith('choice:')?document.querySelector(`[data-focus-choice="${focus.slice(7)}"]`):focus.startsWith('plan:')?document.querySelector(`[data-focus-plan="${focus.slice(5)}"]`):document.getElementById(focus);if(el&&!el.disabled)el.focus({preventScroll:true});else if(t.mode==='order'||t.mode==='route')document.querySelector('[data-focus-choice]:not(:disabled)')?.focus({preventScroll:true});}
}
function focusFinish(){const s=focusState,d=focusGames[s.index];focusProgress[s.index]={explored:true};focusSave();app.innerHTML=`<section class="game-wrap friendly-play focus-play"><div class="completion-friend">${friendlyMascot()}</div><h1>A little step together.</h1><p>${d.away}</p><p>You can keep the helpful reminders and support. There is no need to do more now.</p><div class="calm-controls"><button class="secondary" id="focusAgain">Explore this again</button><button class="primary" id="focusReturn">Choose another game →</button></div><p class="micro">Explored, not assessed. No concentration or ADHD symptom score is saved.</p></section>`;focusNav();document.querySelector('#focusAgain').onclick=()=>focusIntro(s.index);document.querySelector('#focusReturn').onclick=focusHome;window.scrollTo(0,0);}
